{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST parse Rust, Python, TypeScript, CSS, Markdown, TOML, and YAML\nsources with pinned tree-sitter grammars, selected by file extension. Every\nother text file MUST use a plain-text profile in which each line that is not\nblank is an anonymous outline node of kind `line`. Each supported language MUST\nhave an outline profile that maps grammar node kinds to short outline kind names\nand, for each mapped kind, states whether a node is named, and by which fields\nor children, or anonymous. Only mapped kinds MUST appear in the outline; other\nnodes MUST be transparent, so their outline descendants appear under the\nnearest outline ancestor. A profile MAY attach grammar siblings to an outline\nnode, such as Rust attributes and doc comments preceding an item, so the outline\ntree need not match the grammar tree exactly; attached siblings are part of that\nnode for its line range and hash. Every file's outline MUST have a root node\nfor the whole file, independent of language. Source in no other outline node,\nsuch as top-level statements no profile maps, MUST belong to the root node;\nprofiles MUST NOT invent fallback kinds for it. Comments MUST NOT be outline nodes. Profiles MUST be\ndocumented. Upgrading a grammar or profile MAY change outlines and MUST be\ntreated as a deliberate change.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the sources satisfy `requirements.references.outlines`. I found no gaps and no FIXME acknowledgements.\n\n**Implementation, by obligation**\n- **Pinned grammars and extension selection.**\n  - `Cargo.toml` pins `tree-sitter` and each grammar crate with `=` versions (rust 0.24.2, python 0.25.0, typescript 0.23.2, css 0.25.0, md 0.5.4, toml-ng 0.7.0, yaml 0.7.2).\n  - `profile::profiles()` and `profile_for_path` (`src/outline/profile.rs`) choose the profile by lowercased file extension.\n  - Every other path falls back to `plain::PROFILE`.\n  - `outline::parse` and `parse_with` (`src/outline/mod.rs`) run the grammar and report syntax errors with a line number through `check_errors`.\n- **Plain-text profile.** `plain_text` in `src/outline/mod.rs` emits one anonymous `line` node per non-blank line.\n- **Per-language profiles.**\n  - Each profile has a kind table of `KindRule` rows (grammar kind → short kind → `NameRule`) in `rust.rs`, `python.rs`, `typescript.rs` (plus TSX), `css.rs`, `markdown.rs`, `toml.rs` and `yaml.rs`.\n  - `NameRule` expresses named-by-field, named-by-first-child, custom, or anonymous.\n- **Transparency and root.**\n  - `Builder::walk` recurses into unmapped grammar nodes with the same parent, so their descendants appear under the nearest outline ancestor.\n  - `root_node` creates a root for every file, with an empty kind and selector and a range covering the whole file.\n  - Source that no profile maps stays in the root, and no fallback kinds exist. The profile tables contain only the documented kinds.\n- **Attached siblings.**\n  - `Profile::attaches`, with the Rust attribute and outer-doc rule and the Python decorator rule, feeds `Draft::attached`.\n  - `finish` extends `line_start` over the attached siblings, and `hash` includes them.\n- **Comments are not outline nodes.** `Builder::maps` excludes anything `is_comment` reports as a comment, and each profile defines its own `is_comment`.\n- **Documentation and deliberate upgrades.** `md/reference.md` (\"Outline profiles\", lines ~400–457) has a full profile table and per-language details. It also states that grammar versions are pinned exactly and that an upgrade or profile change is deliberate.\n\n**Marking.** The structures and functions implementing the requirement carry `{impl}`.\n- The Rust helpers `impl_name`, `extern_name`, `item_macro` and `in_item_list` are marked only `rust_item_selectors`. That requirement specifies those naming rules, so I do not count this as a gap.\n- `has_marker`, `is_doc_comment` and `doc_prose` are marked `structural_hash`.\n- `never` and `whole_comment` are marked `structural_hash`.\n\n**Tests** (`src/outline/tests.rs` and `src/authoring/tools.rs`)\n- `plain_text_lines_are_interchangeable_anonymous_nodes`: plain text.\n- `reports_parse_failures_with_lines`: parse errors.\n- `python_profile_outlines_defs_classes_and_statements`: Python, including top-level statements falling to the root.\n- `typescript_profile_outlines_declarations`: TypeScript and TSX.\n- `css_profile_names_rules_by_normalized_selectors`: CSS, including unmapped `@import` and comments.\n- `markdown_profile_nests_sections_by_heading`: Markdown, including the HTML comment and reflow-stable hashes.\n- `toml_and_yaml_profiles_name_keys`: TOML and YAML.\n- `file_level_inner_doc_comments_and_unmapped_code_belong_to_the_root`: root-ownership cases, including Markdown front matter.\n- `no_profile_invents_fallback_kinds`: no fallback kinds across all languages.\n- `line_queries_find_innermost_and_declared_nodes`: Rust nesting and same-line siblings.\n- `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs` (`src/authoring/tools.rs`): the outline tool end to end, including a doc comment on a struct and a plain-text file.\n- I did not trace dedicated Rust attribute-attachment tests. The supplied tests do cover the struct doc comment, and attached-sibling line ranges are covered by `selector_raw_lines` and related tests under other requirements.",
